# Copy to .env.local for local development overrides (gitignored).
#
# GBSERVER_API_URL
#   Base URL of a running gbserver instance.
#
#   Dev mode (yarn dev):
#     Enables the API proxy — all /api/* requests are forwarded server-side to this
#     URL, so there are no CORS issues. Optional: if unset, the UI loads but all data
#     pages show empty states (useful for pure UI development without a backend).
#
#   Standalone mode (make build-frontend):
#     Baked into the bundle at build time. Overrides the default same-origin path.
#     Leave unset when gbserver serves the frontend at the same origin (the default).
#
# GBSERVER_API_URL=http://localhost:8080

# MONACO_VS_PATH
#   Where the reward-function code editor loads the Monaco assets from.
#
#   Unset (the default), @monaco-editor/react fetches Monaco from jsdelivr at
#   runtime, so the editor never appears in an air-gapped or egress-restricted
#   deployment. Point this at a self-hosted copy of Monaco's `vs` directory to
#   work offline. Only @monaco-editor/react is a dependency here, not the
#   `monaco-editor` package that carries those assets, so obtain them separately
#   (e.g. `npm pack monaco-editor` and extract `package/min/vs`) and serve them
#   from apps/standalone/public — say public/monaco/vs for the value below.
#
#   Baked into the bundle at build time, so it must be set for the build:
#     MONACO_VS_PATH=/monaco/vs make build-frontend
#
# MONACO_VS_PATH=/monaco/vs
